### Real-time Updates (60fps)
Implementation requirements for animations, movement, and visual effects:
- Use requestAnimationFrame for all smooth updates
  ```typescript
  const animate = () => {
    requestAnimationFrame(animate);
    // Update visual state
  };
  ```
- Implement RAF fallback for background tabs
  ```typescript
  const fallback = () => {
    setTimeout(fallback, 1000 / 60);
    // Update visual state
  };
  ```
- Monitor frame rate using Performance.now()
  ```typescript
  let lastFrame = Performance.now();
  const checkFrameRate = () => {
    const now = Performance.now();
    const delta = now - lastFrame;
    if (delta > 20) { // Frame drop detected
      logPerformanceIssue('Frame drop detected', delta);
    }
    lastFrame = now;
  };
  ```

### Speed-based Updates
Implementation requirements for attack animations:
- Calculate duration based on battalion speed
  ```typescript
  const getAttackDuration = (speed: number) => 1000 / speed;
  ```
- Use Animated.timing with proper easing
  ```typescript
  Animated.timing(animatedValue, {
    toValue: 1,
    duration: getAttackDuration(battalion.speed),
    easing: Easing.bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1),
    useNativeDriver: true
  }).start();
  ```
- Ensure consistent pacing across different speeds
  ```typescript
  const normalizeSpeed = (speed: number) => {
    return Math.max(MIN_SPEED, Math.min(MAX_SPEED, speed));
  };
  ```

### Global Timer Integration (1s)
Implementation requirements for health, damage, and state synchronization:
- Align with backend update cycle
  ```typescript
  const SYNC_INTERVAL = 1000; // 1 second
  setInterval(syncWithBackend, SYNC_INTERVAL);
  ```
- Buffer state changes for smooth transitions
  ```typescript
  const stateBuffer = new StateBuffer();
  stateBuffer.push(newState);
  stateBuffer.flush(); // Apply changes on next frame
  ```
- Handle state dependencies
  ```typescript
  const updateQueue = new UpdateQueue();
  updateQueue.addDependency('health', ['damage', 'healing']);
  updateQueue.process();
  ```

### Performance Monitoring
Implementation requirements for timing verification:
- Track frame rate consistency
  ```typescript
  const frameRateMonitor = new FrameRateMonitor();
  frameRateMonitor.start();
  ```
- Log timing issues
  ```typescript
  const logTimingIssue = (type: string, data: any) => {
    console.warn(`Timing issue detected: ${type}`, data);
  };
  ```
- Monitor animation synchronization
  ```typescript
  const syncMonitor = new AnimationSyncMonitor();
  syncMonitor.checkSync();
  ```

